{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Arial;}}\fs22\b Use-Case Flow Specification - Lab 1\b0\par Use Case: Run Daily Audit (WHOIS & SSL Check)\par Primary Actor(s): SysAdmin (system-initiated audit is monitored by the SysAdmin)\par Supporting Actor(s): WHOIS Service, Notification Service\par Goal: Obtain current domain/certificate expiry status and issue alerts before expiration.\par\b Preconditions\b0\par The monitoring engine is configured with at least one monitored domain/SSL endpoint and a valid daily schedule.\par The system can reach the monitored endpoints and the WHOIS service.\par\b Postconditions\b0\par WHOIS and SSL/TLS audit results are updated for monitored endpoints.\par Required alerts are generated and passed to the configured escalation path.\par Audit results and alert activity are stored for later review.\par\b Main Success Scenario\b0\par 1. The scheduler triggers the daily audit at the configured time.\par 2. The system retrieves the current list of monitored domains and SSL endpoints.\par 3. For each domain, the system performs a WHOIS lookup to obtain registration and expiration information.\par 4. For each SSL endpoint, the system performs a TLS handshake and extracts the certificate expiration date.\par 5. The system compares domain and certificate expiry dates with the current date.\par 6. If an expiry is within 30, 15, or 3 days, the system creates the corresponding alert.\par 7. The system stores audit results and generated alerts in the audit/history records.\par 8. The system sends alerts through the configured escalation ladder.\par 9. The audit completes and the dashboard reflects the latest status.\par\b Alternate Flow A - External Service Unavailable\b0\par A1. WHOIS service or a monitored SSL endpoint is unreachable or times out.\par A2. The system retries the request using the configured retry/timeout policy.\par A3. If the retry still fails, the system records the audit item as failed and continues with the remaining endpoints.\par A4. The system records the failure for review and, where configured, notifies the SysAdmin.\par\b Alternate Flow B - Alert Acknowledged\b0\par B1. A recipient acknowledges the alert.\par B2. The system records the acknowledgement and stops further escalation for that alert.}